From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alpha-liu-01 <116528196+alpha-liu-01@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] apparmor: af_unix: pass the lock class to
 unix_state_lock_nested()

In this 5.4.283 tree, unix_state_lock_nested() takes a lock class
(enum unix_socket_lock_class, from a stable backport). The af_unix
mediation patch keeps its own copy of unix_state_double_lock() from older
kernels and no longer builds. Pass U_LOCK_SECOND, as net/unix/af_unix.c
does for the second socket.
---
diff --git a/security/apparmor/af_unix.c b/security/apparmor/af_unix.c
--- a/security/apparmor/af_unix.c
+++ b/security/apparmor/af_unix.c
@@ -580,10 +580,10 @@
 	}
 	if (sk1 < sk2) {
 		unix_state_lock(sk1);
-		unix_state_lock_nested(sk2);
+		unix_state_lock_nested(sk2, U_LOCK_SECOND);
 	} else {
 		unix_state_lock(sk2);
-		unix_state_lock_nested(sk1);
+		unix_state_lock_nested(sk1, U_LOCK_SECOND);
 	}
 }
 
--

